b:
The minute you learn that Amy was a pageant girl, you will understand. The whole girly drama, behind-the-back talking, and idea that she \*must\* get along with everyone (even if its fake and surface level) is ingrained in her blood.

&amp;#x200B;

She just cannot wrap her head around the fact that Lucie is a tomboy type and doesn't subscribe to Amy's way of life and friendship. Lucie just wants to have fun, workout, and be silly. Amy wants her to huddle around the beanbags and stir drama. You couldn't have found two girls who are further apart.

&amp;#x200B;

THE ONLY PROBLEM here is that when Lucie seems to get the fact that they are different, but Amy doesn't accept who she is and is trying to change her to become someone like her. Everything we have seen is Amy bullying and manipulating Lucie to change her actions and behaviors. Why should anyone change who they are to please you? Lucie during all of this has never insulted or done Amy wrong. This whole situation has been started and continued by Amy because Lucie chooses to spend time with other people.

She 100% deserves it. One of the most immature and fake contestants on the show.

&amp;#x200B;

She sees Danny chatting with Arabella. "Oh, Im going to sit on his lap and be affectionate for 3min and then come back guys." to Amber and Michael. What a fake calculated human being.

&amp;#x200B;

Imagine Lucie needing to say that about Joe or any other real couple. She is just not a good person and has no real love for Danny. Literally using him as an object and her ticket to stay in the villa.

I wouldn't ever be that rude even arguing with the wife, let alone someone who I have only known for two weeks. She is acting way out of hand. There is no realistic context on Love Island where that is acceptable.

&amp;#x200B;

Just look at how mature and calm Danny and Arabella were.
